Z||000000||William Federle||03-20-2000||07:11 PM||||My Fiero leaves a green puddle under it when I get home after driving long enough for the thermostat to open up. I tried to forstall the inevitable by using various stop-leak products but to no avail. I guess it's time for a new radiator. The water pump coincidentally started making noise - most noticible at idle. I think my car is getting to the point where almost everything is wearing out at once (about 190K).<P>Does anyone know of anything special I should know before starting work on replacing the radiator and water pump?<P><p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 03-20-2000).]||||reg||1
